  {
   "id": 631810,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p>Here is a graph of <span data-math=\"y= f(x)\">y= f(x)</span> where <span data-math=\"f(x) = 3x+2\">f(x) = 3x+2</span>.</p>\n<p><img alt=\"GRAPH OF AN EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTION WITH A \\(y\\)-intercepts OF 1 AND PASSING THROUGH THE POINTS 1 COMMA 2, 2 COMMA 4, AND 3 COMMA 8.\" class=\"img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"295\" src=\"exercises/media/f46045af58753018.jpg\" width=\"300\"></p>\n<p>How do the values of <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> change whenever <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 2?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1222848,
     "content_html": "The values of <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> increase by 1 whenever <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 2."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222851,
     "content_html": "The values of <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> increase by 6 whenever <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 2."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222849,
     "content_html": "The values of <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> increase by 3 whenever <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 2."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222850,
     "content_html": "The values of <span data-math=\"f\">f</span> increase by 2 whenever <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> increases by 2."
    }
   ],
